00:27:05.265 --> 00:27:07.745
like they did for our last planet conservation,

00:27:07.745 --> 00:27:11.505
but it shows that our population will continue to decline

00:27:12.090 --> 00:27:13.770
for the foreseeable future.

00:27:15.130 --> 00:27:17.530
And that's what I said to myself,

00:27:19.610 --> 00:27:20.410
you know,

00:27:21.050 --> 00:27:23.930
we need to tackle this affordable housing

00:27:24.185 --> 00:27:26.025
thing. There's people

00:27:26.345 --> 00:27:26.985
that,

00:27:28.105 --> 00:27:38.345
you know, they just can't afford to live in Andover anymore for a lot of different reasons, and we don't have the facilities here. And we've known that for a long time, long term study group,

00:27:39.050 --> 00:27:41.930
you know, in the last plan of conservation development

00:27:42.010 --> 00:27:45.210
highlighted the fact that we needed affordable housing.

00:27:45.690 --> 00:27:50.410
But if people keep moving away from Andover because they can't afford to live here,

00:27:51.130 --> 00:27:52.490
I don't think that's

00:27:52.490 --> 00:28:01.465
a very good thing for us. So I wanted to show you this, maybe everybody was aware of that, but it caught me by surprise. I assumed we were slowly increasing

00:28:01.705 --> 00:28:03.865
and had a healthy population there.

00:28:04.025 --> 00:28:06.265
And this is what made me want to tackle

00:28:06.665 --> 00:28:07.785
the affordable

00:28:07.785 --> 00:28:08.105
housing.

00:28:09.720 --> 00:28:12.680
And since we finished the plan, you know, inflation's

00:28:12.680 --> 00:28:15.080
going up, interest rates are going up, the

00:28:16.760 --> 00:28:22.040
need for affordable housing in town only continues to go up. So hopefully that

00:28:22.575 --> 00:28:23.615
will whet your

00:28:23.775 --> 00:28:26.015
appetite on that. And

00:28:26.575 --> 00:28:30.655
if there's no questions on what the population trends are telling us,

00:28:31.535 --> 00:28:34.335
and it could be that, you know, it doesn't come to pass.

