Any questions on that?

00:29:07.490 --> 00:29:11.490
>> No, I think you're good on the demographics end, Jay. Okay, and so

00:29:11.730 --> 00:29:13.490
>> now I'm going to try and

00:29:13.890 --> 00:29:15.330
go out of this one

00:29:18.530 --> 00:29:20.290
and see if I can get.

00:29:25.295 --> 00:29:27.295
So, the thing that

00:29:27.775 --> 00:29:29.695
you'll be seeing soon

00:29:30.815 --> 00:29:34.335
is one of the actions that comes out of

00:29:34.895 --> 00:29:36.735
the Public Act 2129

00:29:36.735 --> 00:29:38.255
is they had some regulations

00:29:38.550 --> 00:29:42.150
for accessory dwelling units. And part of our plan

00:29:42.390 --> 00:29:44.950
that we'll talk about here in a minute is

00:29:45.830 --> 00:29:52.710
the Planning and Zoning Commission, as well as, you know, in the plan recommends opting out of those regulations.

00:29:59.915 --> 00:30:02.875
So, why do we want to opt out? The

00:30:02.875 --> 00:30:05.195
public act requires each town,

00:30:05.995 --> 00:30:09.410
and I'm just going to read the underlying portion here,

00:30:09.810 --> 00:30:17.490
provided at least one accessory apartment shall be allowed as of right on each lot that contains a single family dwelling.

00:30:19.010 --> 00:30:23.995
And the thing that makes that tough for Andover is if all our lots were,

00:30:24.155 --> 00:30:29.675
you know, one or two acres or bigger, you could put an accessory dwelling unit on there

00:30:29.915 --> 00:30:34.795
and no big deal. But around Andover Lake in Lake District, you know, we've got

00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.860
some very small lots.

00:30:38.300 --> 00:30:43.340
And if we were to say that as of right, each property owner had

00:30:44.380 --> 00:30:48.585
the right to build an accessory unit on there, I think that would be detrimental

00:30:48.585 --> 00:30:54.105
to the health of Andover Lake. And we're all working to kind of keep that lake healthy.

00:30:56.185 --> 00:30:56.745
So,

00:30:57.625 --> 00:30:58.585
our

00:30:58.585 --> 00:31:01.270
current accessory dwelling unit regulations,

00:31:01.270 --> 00:31:05.510
and I don't know if every town's got them already, if that's why they

00:31:05.510 --> 00:31:08.310
don't, and that's why it was put into that public act.

00:31:09.350 --> 00:31:11.350
But we've got regulations

00:31:11.350 --> 00:31:13.910
in effect today that address

00:31:14.085 --> 00:31:15.845
accessory dwelling units.

00:31:17.125 --> 00:31:25.685
For the Lake Ridge District, it talks about if you've got a lot greater than three acres in size, you can put in an accessory dwelling unit.

00:31:27.190 --> 00:31:32.150
We already talked about Andover having several small lots and that not conducive

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:34.310
to the water quality there.

00:31:35.110 --> 00:31:43.855
So anyhow, based on that, you know, our plan was to opt out of that, which is written into the public act. This was the only piece in there that

00:31:44.175 --> 00:31:46.735
we had the opportunity to opt out of.

00:31:47.375 --> 00:31:50.895
And in the process goes the planning and zoning commission

00:31:51.070 --> 00:31:54.590
by two thirds vote votes to initiate the opt out process.

00:31:54.990 --> 00:31:58.510
And I'm hoping to do that at our Planning and Zoning meeting next week.

00:32:00.910 --> 00:32:04.605
After that's done, we're required to hold a public hearing on

00:32:04.765 --> 00:32:08.125
the opting out of it to get input from the town.

00:32:09.165 --> 00:32:12.445
And if the commission decides to opt out within

00:32:12.445 --> 00:32:13.165
statutory

00:32:13.965 --> 00:32:14.845
deadlines,

00:32:15.645 --> 00:32:22.680
sixty five days after the close of hearing, we need to state on the record the reasons for the decision that takes two thirds vote to approve.

00:32:23.080 --> 00:32:26.280
We've got to publish our notice of decision like we always do.

00:32:28.040 --> 00:32:31.080
And then we get to the Board of Selectmen. So once

00:32:31.795 --> 00:32:34.995
once we have done that, we bring it to the Board of Selectmen,

00:32:35.395 --> 00:32:39.795
and it needs to be ratified by a two thirds vote of the town's legislative

00:32:39.795 --> 00:32:40.355
body

00:32:40.675 --> 00:32:44.115
or its Board of Selectmen if the town meeting is legislative body.

00:32:45.040 --> 00:32:47.200
And I'm under the impression that the

00:32:47.600 --> 00:32:52.080
town meeting is the legislative body for our town so we should be able to

00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:55.920
ratify that by a two thirds vote of the board of selectman.

00:32:56.575 --> 00:33:00.655
But I didn't want to come to the Board of Selectmen with this being a done deal

00:33:00.815 --> 00:33:06.575
having it be the first that you heard about it. And so that's why I wanted to come

00:33:07.055 --> 00:33:08.095
to you here tonight.

00:33:09.230 --> 00:33:10.590
If we don't do that,

00:33:11.310 --> 00:33:12.990
all the requirements

00:33:13.070 --> 00:33:15.630
of the Public Act go into effect

00:33:16.030 --> 00:33:29.215
regardless of what our regulations say. So at that point, our regulations are null and void. State regulations are there and they allow anybody that wants to endow to build at least one accessory unit on their property.

00:33:31.055 --> 00:33:36.495
And then, you know, there were some good ideas in that public act. We might want to change

00:33:37.050 --> 00:33:37.530
our

00:33:38.090 --> 00:33:52.490
accessory dwelling unit regulations at some point in the future. But at this point, I just wanted to make sure that we got the opt out process complete before the end of the year so that we had the opportunity to take what we wanted from the state's recommendations

00:33:52.805 --> 00:33:54.565
and not be forced to

00:33:55.125 --> 00:33:55.845
allow

00:33:56.245 --> 00:33:59.685
